  /* KENYA'S FLAGSHIP HOSPITALITY COLLEGE HAD ONE RECORD IN A CATALOGUE OF 301.
   *
   * Utalii offers 13 diploma and certificate programmes and, from March 2026,
   * is placed through KUCCPS for the first time in its history - 765 students
   * in the 2026 cycle. Njia listed a single course, priced it off a fee regime
   * that does not apply to it, and called that verified.
   *
   * The Kilifi campus below is new: Ronald Ngala Utalii College takes its
   * pioneer intake of roughly 1,000 learners in September 2026, with KUCCPS
   * applications closing 23 August 2026. Kilifi had one private college in this
   * catalogue until now, in a county whose economy runs on hospitality.
   *
   * Note the entry grades. Hospitality is widely treated as the place you go
   * when your grades disappoint; Utalii asks a C plain for a diploma and a C-
   * for a certificate, which is stricter than the public-TVET ladder. Showing
   * that plainly is more useful than letting the assumption stand. */
